Rain runoff suspended sediment loss t/ha by treatments Wallumbilla catchment study 1982 -1997
//Data type: Daily Rainfall (mm), Runoff (mm) Soil Movement (t/ha), Suspended sediment concentration (mg/L), Suspended sediment load (t/ha) for four winter crop-fallow treatments (stubble burnt, incorporated, mulch, zero tillage) and a summer crop
//Continuous data - zero values means no observable variable, not missing data. -continuous data infilled (tilled only) and date corrected
//Soil loss/erosion represents movement of soil to the bottom of the cultivated plane Suspended sediment concentration was determined at the weir outlet and sediment load calculated from a flow weighted mean concentration and runoff depth (Freebairn and Wockner 1986)
//Possible timing errors of +-1 day between some observations.
//
//Data source: Data was compiled from field notes and hydrologic databases (RRUMS, Hydstra) by David Freebairn and Graeme Wockner, Queensland Department of Natural Resources 2007 and revised in 2021
//This datafile is based on or contains data provided by the State of Queensland (Department of Environment and Resource Management) 2012.
//© The State of Queensland (Department of Environment and Resource Management) 2012.
